    <!-- EDITORIAL & SCIENTIFIC DERIVATION ARTICLE -->
    <article style="border-top: 1px solid #e2e8f0; padding-top: 3.5rem; line-height: 1.85; color: #334155;">
      
      <h2 style="font-size: clamp(1.4rem, 3.5vw, 1.85rem); font-weight: 800; color: #0f172a; margin-bottom: 1rem; letter-spacing: -0.02em; line-height: 1.3;">
        Mathematical Foundations of the Brunauer–Emmett–Teller (BET) Model
      </h2>
      <p>
        The Brunauer–Emmett–Teller (BET) equation represents the definitive IUPAC standard for determining the specific surface area of finely divided, porous, and nanostructured materials. Developed in 1938 as a generalized statistical extension of the Langmuir monolayer model, it accounts for infinite multimolecular condensation on solid surfaces with the key premise that layers beyond the first exhibit liquid-like condensation thermodynamics:
      </p>
      
      <div style="background: #f8fafc; border: 1px solid #e2e8f0; border-radius: 10px; padding: 1.25rem 2rem; margin: 1.5rem 0; text-align: center; box-shadow: inset 0 1px 2px rgba(0,0,0,0.02); overflow-x: auto;">
        <div style="font-size: clamp(1rem, 2.5vw, 1.35rem); font-weight: 800; color: #0f172a; letter-spacing: 0.05em; font-family: 'Times New Roman', Times, serif; white-space: nowrap;">
          1 / [ V<sub>a</sub> &middot; ((P<sub>0</sub>/P) &minus; 1) ] = [ (C &minus; 1) / (V<sub>m</sub> &middot; C) ] &middot; (P/P<sub>0</sub>) + [ 1 / (V<sub>m</sub> &middot; C) ]
        </div>
      </div>

      <p>
        When plotted as <em>1 / [ V<sub>a</sub> &middot; ((P<sub>0</sub>/P) &minus; 1) ]</em> versus <em>P/P<sub>0</sub></em>, the relationship yields a straight line with slope <em>s = (C &minus; 1) / (V<sub>m</sub> &middot; C)</em> and y-intercept <em>i = 1 / (V<sub>m</sub> &middot; C)</em>. From these empirical parameters, the monolayer capacity <em>V<sub>m</sub></em> and the dimensionless energetic constant <em>C</em> are resolved:
      </p>

      <div style="display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(min(100%, 240px), 1fr)); gap: 1rem; margin: 1.5rem 0;">
        <div style="background: #ffffff; border: 1px solid #cbd5e1; border-radius: 8px; padding: 1rem; text-align: center;">
          <strong style="color: #64748b; font-size: 0.8rem; text-transform: uppercase; display: block; margin-bottom: 0.35rem;">Monolayer Capacity (V<sub>m</sub>)</strong>
          <span style="font-family: monospace; font-size: 1.15rem; font-weight: 800; color: #0284c7;">V<sub>m</sub> = 1 / (s + i)</span>
        </div>
        <div style="background: #ffffff; border: 1px solid #cbd5e1; border-radius: 8px; padding: 1rem; text-align: center;">
          <strong style="color: #64748b; font-size: 0.8rem; text-transform: uppercase; display: block; margin-bottom: 0.35rem;">BET Energetic Constant (C)</strong>
          <span style="font-family: monospace; font-size: 1.15rem; font-weight: 800; color: #0284c7;">C = 1 + (s / i)</span>
        </div>
        <div style="background: #ffffff; border: 1px solid #cbd5e1; border-radius: 8px; padding: 1rem; text-align: center;">
          <strong style="color: #64748b; font-size: 0.8rem; text-transform: uppercase; display: block; margin-bottom: 0.35rem;">Specific Surface Area (S<sub>BET</sub>)</strong>
          <span style="font-family: monospace; font-size: 1.15rem; font-weight: 800; color: #059669;">S<sub>BET</sub> = (V<sub>m</sub> &middot; N<sub>A</sub> &middot; &sigma;) / V<sub>mol</sub></span>
        </div>
      </div>

